  "name": "Fontaine's Weapon Modding Quality Of Life",
  "slug": "fontaines-weapon-modding-quality-of-life",
  "teaser": "Out of raid, let's you use the modding screen, inspect and detach/attach weapon mods of weapons that are equipped. In raid, it let's you inspect weapon mods of equipped weapons, and if you have a multitool it lets you detach/attach any weapon mod.",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/1188.png",
  "downloads": 20584,
  "favourites_count": 0,
  "description": "<p><strong>Fontaine’s Weapon Modding Quality Of Life</strong></p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zF\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zF</a>_YexoLMK0</p>\n<p><strong>This mod is no longer being maintained, it is now part of Tyfon’s UI fixes mod! <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1860-ui-fixes/#versions\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1860-ui-fixes/#versions</a></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Out of Raid:</strong></p>\n<p>You can attach/detach vital parts of weapons that are in your equipment slots (primary, secondary, holster) and use the preset and modding screen.</p>\n<p><strong>In Raid:</strong></p>\n<p>You can inspect all weapon parts of weapons in your equipment slots, and if you have a multitool and the weapon is not in your equipment slots you can attach/detach any parts. There is a config option to disable the multitool requirement.</p>\n<p><strong>Issues:</strong></p>\n<p>There may be unforeseen bugs and issues, let me know if you encounter them</p>\n",
